\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Study design. We train six byte-level BPE tokenizers (8,192 entries each) that differ only in merge order. Four change the \emph  {learning order}, which changes the vocabulary. Two keep \textsc  {Freq}\xspace  's exact merges and change only the \emph  {application order}, i.e.,\xspace  merge priority at encoding time. Every tokenizer is paired with an identical language model trained on the same text, and we evaluate it with tokenizer-independent bits-per-byte and with fine-tuned classification.\relax }}{2}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{2}{Study design. We train six byte-level BPE tokenizers (8,192 entries each) that differ only in merge order. Four change the \emph {learning order}, which changes the vocabulary. Two keep \freq 's exact merges and change only the \emph {application order}, \ie merge priority at encoding time. Every tokenizer is paired with an identical language model trained on the same text, and we evaluate it with tokenizer-independent bits-per-byte and with fine-tuned classification.\relax }{figure.caption.2}{}}
