\newlabel{tab:robustness}{{5}{9}{Robustness to the random draw. A second draw (\textsc {-t1}) of each random tokenizer, trained with pre-training seed 0, gives effects of the same size as the first draw. $\Delta $ is relative to \freq seed 0. Accuracy (\%) is the mean of 2 fine-tuning seeds on the seed-0 model; differences between draws are within 0.7 points on every task.\relax }{table.caption.9}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces The four hypotheses we set out to test and their verdicts. The qualitative ordering largely holds for BPB\xspace  , but the hypothesized effect sizes are too large, and none of the effects reaches fine-tuned accuracy.\relax }}{9}{table.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:hypotheses}{{6}{9}{The four hypotheses we set out to test and their verdicts. The qualitative ordering largely holds for \bpb , but the hypothesized effect sizes are too large, and none of the effects reaches fine-tuned accuracy.\relax }{table.caption.10}{}}
